  "worked_solution": "Let $({x}_{m},{y}_{m})$ be the midpoint between ${{(-9p,3q)}_{\u23df}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{1}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{1})}$ and ${{(6p,5q)}_{\u23df}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{2}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{2})}.$\n\nWe use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}_{m},{y}_{m}) & =(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{-9p+6p}{2},\\frac{3q+5q}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{-3p}{2},\\frac{8q}{2}) \\\\  & =(-\\frac{3p}{2},4q)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
